{"event_id": "ed65a907-e75f-4f53-bb0d-13c33b39007a", "event_type": "assistant_message_completed", "payload": {"citations": [], "content": "**Bug found and fixed.**\n\nIn `prices.py`, `sum_prices` accumulated the total with `total -= price` (subtraction) instead of addition, so any input produced the negated sum (e.g. `[2, 3, 7]` → `-12`).\n\n**Change made** (only `prices.py`):\n```python\ndef sum_prices(prices):\n    total = 0\n    for price in prices:\n        total += price\n    return total\n```\n\n**Verification result (actual):** I ran `python.exe verify.py` with the specified interpreter. It exited with code 0 and printed `Verification passed` on stdout (stderr empty). So all three assertions in `verify.py` (`sum_prices([2, 3, 7]) == 12`, `sum_prices([]) == 0`, `sum_prices([-1, 4]) == 3`) now hold.\n\nNote: `notes.txt` also mentions `sum_prices` but is not implementation code, so I left it untouched.", "model_supplement": "", "tool_calls": []}, "schema_version": 3, "sequence": 39, "session_id": "515d875f-2257-4cd9-afb9-38bd21c0bca6", "timestamp": "2026-09-23T12:00:31.620110+00:00", "turn_id": "ca6dbc56-a594-4730-a8b9-7464501538b4"}
